  "id": "cda8139e-95af-56da-ae52-4d1868244681",
  "slug": "chef-john-s-easter-breakfast-casserole-recipe-11924673",
  "name": "Chef John\u2019s Easter Breakfast Casserole",
  "recipe_type": "breakfast",
  "brief_description": "Chef John's Easter breakfast casserole is the lightest, most tender, perfectly-textured egg casserole you will ever make. It has the perfect ratio of eggs and milk to create a feather-light custard, and friendly bite-sized pieces of spring vegetables and ham.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Cut tips off asparagus and then slice spears into 1-inch pieces. Transfer into generously salted, boiling water and stir. Wait a minute or two for the water to just start boiling again, stirring occasionally. Remove asparagus with a strainer into cold water. Once chilled, drain well and set aside. Slice ham into thin, 1-inch pieces and reserve."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Carefully add potatoes to the boiling water and cook until tender, 15 to 20 minutes. Drain well and set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Add olive oil to a pan and set over medium-high heat. Saute onions and peppers with a large pinch of salt until the onions just turn translucent, and soften slightly, about 5 minutes. Let cool and reserve."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "For custard, whisk eggs together in a bowl; once eggs are fairly uniform, whisk in milk, cream, salt, pepper, and cayenne."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C). Oil a 13x9-inch casserole pan. Cut potatoes into bite-sized pieces, and arrange evenly on the bottom of the pan. Scatter over half the cheese, then half the onion-pepper mixture. Top evenly with ham and asparagus, being careful not to press down. Top with the rest of the onion-pepper mixture."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Pour egg custard mixture in carefully; top with the rest of the cheese. Jiggle the pan and tap gently a few times on the counter to settle the custard into all the open spaces."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until eggs are just set, 50 to 60 minutes. Let cool for 10 minutes before serving."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 75,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 30,
